{"id":56724,"ord":84,"n_segments":179,"prev":56723,"next":56725,"doc":{"id":"68154","title":"68154_Gus Johnson oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Gus Johnson","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68154/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=68154"},"chapter":"Jay McShann's band","title":"Impression of Jay; the seven-piece band","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"Gus found Jay jolly and lists the seven-piece band: Gene Ramey, Oliver Minor, William Scott, Bob Mabane, Earl Jackson and singer Joe Coleman.","period":"1938","year_from":1938,"year_to":1938,"words":319,"start":[176,13],"end":[179,8],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=68154#s56724","tags":{"places":[{"name":"Kansas City","focus":0,"type":"city"}],"venues":[{"name":"Martin's on the Plaza","focus":0,"city":"Kansas City"}],"bands":[{"name":"Jay McShann Orchestra","focus":1,"leader":"Jay McShann"},{"name":"Specks Red's band","focus":0,"leader":"Spec Redd"}]},"people":[{"name":"Jay McShann","qid":"Q1684347","n":3},{"name":"William Scott","qid":null,"n":3},{"name":"Gene Ramey","qid":"Q727217","n":2},{"name":"Oliver Minor","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Bill Hadnot","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Charlie Parker","qid":"Q103767","n":1},{"name":"Spec Redd","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Earl Jackson","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Bob Mabane","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Joe Coleman","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":34,"theme_name":"Who was in the band: naming sidemen and personnel","community":60,"community_name":"Who played in the band: reciting personnel","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":176,"b":13,"s":"MS.","x":"Well, what was your impression of Jay?"},{"p":176,"b":14,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Oh, he was a fine guy to me. Jolly, you know?"},{"p":176,"b":15,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":176,"b":16,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And -- let's see, when I came back there and Hadnot introduced me to him, one of those things, and he told me about the job that's going to open up out on Martin's-on-the-Plaza. I said, sure, that's the reason why"},{"p":177,"b":0,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"I'm here. I left a job to come here for that. And it was Gene Ramey."},{"p":177,"b":1,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh, I see, Billy Hadnot didn't go in the band."},{"p":177,"b":2,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"No, he didn't go in. I thought Billy was going to make it, but he didn't make it."},{"p":177,"b":3,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":177,"b":4,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And pretty soon he had to go in the Army, anyway, see."},{"p":177,"b":5,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh, yeah."},{"p":177,"b":6,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"So it was Gene Ramey, myself, Oliver Minor, William Scott, --"},{"p":177,"b":7,"s":"MS.","x":"What did he play?"},{"p":177,"b":8,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Scott?"},{"p":177,"b":9,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":177,"b":10,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Tenor."},{"p":177,"b":11,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh, yeah."},{"p":177,"b":12,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Bob Mabane on tenor."},{"p":177,"b":13,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":177,"b":14,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And Earl Jackson, alto."},{"p":177,"b":15,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh."},{"p":177,"b":16,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"See, this was before Charlie Parker."},{"p":177,"b":17,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah, right, right."},{"p":177,"b":18,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And Jay who you know."},{"p":177,"b":19,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":178,"b":0,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"We had seven pieces."},{"p":178,"b":1,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":178,"b":2,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And --"},{"p":178,"b":3,"s":"MS.","x":"You had three saxophones? Three reeds?"},{"p":178,"b":4,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Yes. Two tenors, an alto and --"},{"p":178,"b":5,"s":"MS.","x":"And one trumpet?"},{"p":178,"b":6,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And one trumpet?"},{"p":178,"b":7,"s":"MS.","x":"Who was?"},{"p":178,"b":8,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Oliver Minor. Little Piggy."},{"p":178,"b":9,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh, I see."},{"p":178,"b":10,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And myself and Jay."},{"p":178,"b":11,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh, that was a good --"},{"p":178,"b":12,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And we had a singer with us, too. His name was Coleman -- Joe Coleman."},{"p":178,"b":13,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh. Well, who was writing for that, three saxophones and a trumpet?"},{"p":178,"b":14,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Hm?"},{"p":178,"b":15,"s":"MS.","x":"Who was writing?"},{"p":178,"b":16,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"William Scott."},{"p":178,"b":17,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh. I see."},{"p":178,"b":18,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"He's a Good arranger, a very good arranger."},{"p":178,"b":19,"s":"MS.","x":"And so that little band must have swung."},{"p":178,"b":20,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Oh, it was a swinging little band."},{"p":178,"b":21,"s":"MS.","x":"Was that the best band you'd been in,"},{"p":179,"b":0,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"For a small band?"},{"p":179,"b":1,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":179,"b":2,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"To me, yes."},{"p":179,"b":3,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":179,"b":4,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Yes, very much so."},{"p":179,"b":5,"s":"MS.","x":"Jay -- you know --"},{"p":179,"b":6,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Spec's band was very good. It was very good."},{"p":179,"b":7,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh, it was, yeah."},{"p":179,"b":8,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"We had the three saxes in and that made it much better."}]}